# LambdaForge — Code Ownership
#
# This file declares who's responsible for reviewing changes to different
# parts of the codebase. When combined with branch protection rules on
# `main` ("Require review from Code Owners"), it ensures that:
#
#   1. PRs to protected paths automatically request review from the
#      relevant owner.
#   2. PRs cannot be merged without at least one code-owner approval.
#
# Syntax: gitignore-style patterns followed by @github-username.
# See: https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default — anything not matched below falls through to the repo owner.
*                           @vishwakt

# ── Trading-critical code ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Changes here can lose real money. Always require owner review, even with
# future collaborators.
/src/risk.py                @vishwakt
/src/scheduler.py           @vishwakt
/src/client.py              @vishwakt
/src/strategies/            @vishwakt
/src/market_hours.py        @vishwakt

# ── Infrastructure / deployment ──────────────────────────────────────────────
/template.yaml              @vishwakt
/Dockerfile                 @vishwakt
/.github/workflows/         @vishwakt
/iam-*-policy.template.json @vishwakt
/samconfig.toml.example     @vishwakt

# ── Security / governance ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
